{
  "pdf_page": 220,
  "book_page": 190,
  "verified_by": "claude-opus-5",
  "verified_on": "2026-09-06",
  "entries": [
    {
      "entry": 0,
      "root": "Hebhel",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "modern_form": "Biblical Hebrew הֶבֶל heḇel 'breath, vapour, vanity'; also the personal name Heḇel (Abel), Gen. 4",
      "note": "Klein s.v. 'Abel' (1966 ed. leaf 13 = pp. 2-3) prints verbatim: 'Abel, masc. PN.; in the Bible, the second son of Adam and Eve. — L., fr. Gk. Ἄβελ, fr. Heb. Hebhel, lit. ‘breath, vanity’.' Nourai's root name, language label and gloss are Klein's own, letter for letter ('Hebhel' = his transliteration of הֶבֶל with spirantised bh = ḇ). Wiktionary adds the one caveat: the personal name is only 'possibly' the homonymous common noun heḇel 'breath, vapour; vanity' (the word of Eccl. 1:2 hăḇēl hăḇālîm) and may instead be Akkadian ablu 'son'; that reservation touches the name, not the Hebrew word, so the root box stands. Note also that Nourai's page numbers for Klein on this page (KLN:496, KLN:694) sit ~4% below the 1966 two-volume pagination (ebony = leaf 270 ≈ p.516; Hagar/hegira = leaves 374/385 ≈ pp.724/746) while KLN:3 is exact — the signature of the compressed 1971 one-volume 'unabridged' reprint, which is evidently the copy he used.",
      "note_fa": "ریشهٔ عبری הֶבֶל (heḇel) به معنای «دم، بخار، بیهودگی» است و در سفر پیدایش (باب ۴) نام دومین پسر آدم و حوا نیز هست. کلاین در مدخل Abel (چاپ ۱۹۶۶، برگ ۱۳ ≈ ص ۳) دقیقاً همین را می‌آورد و بنابراین نام ریشه، برچسب زبانی و معنای آن در نمودار نورایی درست است. تنها نکتهٔ احتیاطی آن است که ویکی‌واژه پیوند نامِ خاص «هابیل» را با اسم عامِ heḇel «دم، بخار» تنها «محتمل» می‌داند و احتمال دیگری (اکدی ablu «پسر») را نیز یاد می‌کند. در مجموع ادعای نورایی دربارهٔ ریشه درست است.",
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Abel"
      ],
      "ref_check": [
        {"ref": "KLN:3", "status": "supports", "note": "KLN_1966.txt line 1150 (leaf 13 = pp.2-3): 'Abel, masc. PN.; in the Bible, the second son of Adam and Eve. — L., fr. Gk. Ἄβελ, fr. Heb. Hebhel, lit. ‘breath, vanity’.' Exactly the root box (grep -n '^Abel,' KLN_1966.txt)."}
      ],
      "consulted": [
        {"src": "KLN", "where": "1966 leaf 13 (pp. 2-3), s.v. Abel; also line 6015 s.v. cable", "stance": "supports", "note": "s.v. 'cable' Klein separately lists 'Heb. hebhel, ‘rope, cord’' as a homonym, confirming that the transliteration Hebhel = הֶבֶל and that Klein keeps the two Hebrew hebhel words apart."},
        {"src": "Wiktionary", "where": "en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Abel", "stance": "partial", "note": "'from Biblical Hebrew הֶבֶל (Héḇel, ‘Abel’), possibly from the homonymous word הֶבֶל (heḇel, ‘breath, vapor; vanity’) or from Akkadian 𒌉𒍑 (ablu, ‘son’)' — same Hebrew etymon, but the 'breath, vanity' sense is flagged as only probable."}
      ],
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "lang": "Arabic",
          "words": "",
